MsgEn:
Heinz and the others did a great job, huh?
The trouble is resolved;
Peace has been restored.

In this situation, I can only hope
for brave actions from Mr. Crow,
who's always hungry for food.

It's about that esteemed figure; 
without a doubt, a magnificent transformation 
will be forthcoming.

It looks like Chief Alchemist 
Diamantes is undertaking a major study; 
I wonder what will unfold.

I can sense the weakening vitality 
of the forest and the land; 
Lestania is faltering.

The gold of the Golden Country does not 
come from the land; 
it is gold born from nothingness.

I consider myself the captain's right-hand man;
No matter who comes back or leaves,
That will never change.

Welcome to Tel.
Let us help you prepare for your journey;
How can we help you?

The <VAL EMNAME> were a bit of a distraction
from my search at <VAL SPOT>,
so I killed about <VAL> of them, Master.

Master, I went to search [<VAL SPOT>];
It was dangerous.
But you see, I have a treasure as a souvenir.

Yes, I've heard the tale; 
you are heading to the new Ark 
that fell into the western sea, correct?

I'm going to Mergoda.
This isn't where I belong;
my place is over there!

I think it might be that she wanted a break,
or perhaps just some time alone;
something along the lines of that.

However, that is the way of nature. 
Back then, Lord White Dragon was nothing special;
but something akin to the wind and the clouds.

No, Mayleaf is safe;
she should be by 
Lord White Dragon's side.

If you can obtain the strength to guard Cecily 
from the Black Knight's malevolent hands, 
I will say no more about Leo.

Do not worry about us; 
We will offer assistance 
to the people of Phindym.

Of course, it is not fear that drives us;
battling Dragons is beyond imagination.
For us, the closest emotion is that of taboo.

We can go out somewhere to 
fight or search for things; 
that's something we can do.

We battle the dragon that stole peace
from this land. I am Quintus,
a caretaker of the Liberation Army.

For me, the peace in Lestania is the top priority;
I want to know as soon as possible
what may happen next.

To summarize the current situation;
while using Rothgill Village as a base 
for diversionary tactics...

With Quintus behind me, unless monsters are falling 
from above--no, no, 
let's not start imagining bad things.

In any case, 
if you invade the Royal Capital Megado, 
you will inevitably be confronted with them.

Thou must not allow harm to befall Phindym;
now is the hour to repay the favor bestowed 
by the Spirit Dragon.

Whilst life doth remain, 
the strife shall endure; 
therefore...

Thou must not make this thy final battle; 
hasten—
to the abyss of Mergoda.

Ugh—
if I wait too long, I'll get even hungrier, 
so please, as soon as you can.

My buddy's fighting on the pier up ahead, 
he's a little wounded, not moving too well; 
give me a hand—!

As for the collapsed well, 
if it could be restored to how it was before, 
I'd have no further complaints.

I told Lorna I might not be back
for a week and left the dining hall to her,
so everything's covered!

Once the Spirit Gauge fills
from attacks or dodges,
<COL ff7575><KCT ELIXIR_CHANGE> activates Attack Boost</COL>!

